# Copy to .env.local. Optional in development, required in production.
#
# The API (`engine/` run by FastAPI) is the one authoritative decision engine. When this is set, the
# comparison, the adviser brief and the profile all come from it, and a failing API shows an error.
# Server-side only: not a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, the browser never calls the API.
# AGROCYCLE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# When it is unset, the web app answers from its own TypeScript copy of the engine, an offline fallback
# that is labelled on every screen it answers. That is fine for `npm run dev`. A production build refuses
# to do it unless you opt in on purpose:
# AGROCYCLE_ALLOW_OFFLINE_ENGINE=true
